	'domain-appraisal-services'    => array(
		'kw'          => 'domain appraisal services',
		'lede'        => 'Our domain appraisal services give you a written price range for a name, based on comparable sales, before you buy, sell or negotiate.',
		'h2'          => 'How domain appraisal services work',
		'body'        => array(
			'A domain appraisal estimates what a name is likely to sell for between a willing buyer and a willing seller. It is an opinion supported by evidence, not a fixed value. Good <strong>domain appraisal services</strong> show that evidence so you can judge the figure yourself.',
			'You need an appraisal before you list a name, before you answer an unsolicited offer, before you make an offer on a name someone else owns, and when a name forms part of a business sale or a dispute.',
			'An appraisal also protects you from your own optimism. Owners often value a name by what it cost them or by one headline sale, and buyers often value it by their budget. Neither tells you what the market will pay.',
			array( 'h3' => 'What domain appraisal services should examine' ),
			array(
				'<strong>Length and spelling:</strong> short names that are easy to say and type sell more readily.',
				'<strong>Extension:</strong> .com carries the widest resale demand; other extensions depend on the market they serve.',
				'<strong>Commercial intent:</strong> whether businesses in a profitable field would want the name.',
				'<strong>Comparable sales:</strong> recorded sales of similar names, adjusted for date and quality.',
				'<strong>History:</strong> past use, any trademark conflict and any record of spam.',
			),
			'Each factor is written down with the comparable sales behind it, so the price range can be checked and challenged.',
			array( 'h3' => 'Automated estimates versus a broker appraisal' ),
			'Automated tools produce a number in seconds from a model of past sales. They are useful as a first signal, but they cannot see who might want the name today, and different tools often give very different figures for the same name.',
			'A broker appraisal adds judgment: which buyers exist for the name, how many of them could pay, and what owners of comparable names have accepted. The result is a range with an opening figure and a realistic target, not a single number.',
			array( 'h3' => 'Pitfalls to avoid' ),
			'Be wary of a valuation tied to a paid listing package, and of any appraisal with no comparable sales attached. A value only means something when a buyer is prepared to pay it.',
			'An appraisal describes a likely range at one point in time. Demand for a keyword can rise or fall, so refresh an appraisal that is more than a year old before you rely on it.',
			'Our domain appraisal services follow the same method as any negotiation at Domain Brothers: research first, in writing. A broker replies within one business day.',
			'If you then decide to buy or sell, our <a href="/domain-brokerage-services/">domain brokerage services</a> take it from there. Recent results are on the <a href="/sold/">sold</a> page.',
		),
		'steps'       => 'broker',
		'steps_title' => 'How an appraisal works, in four steps',
		'link'        => array( 'https://www.uspto.gov/trademarks/search', 'the USPTO trademark search', 'Before valuing a name, check it for registered trademarks with' ),
