	'domain-transfer'              => array(
		'kw'          => 'domain transfer',
		'lede'        => 'A domain transfer moves a name from one registrar to another, or from a seller to a buyer, using an EPP code and the ICANN transfer rules.',
		'h2'          => 'How a domain transfer works',
		'body'        => array(
			'There are two kinds of <strong>domain transfer</strong>. A registrar transfer moves a name you own to a different registrar. A change of registrant gives the name to a new owner, which is what happens after a sale. A sale often involves both.',
			'For a registrar transfer, the current registrar issues an authorization code, known as an EPP code. The new registrar uses that code to request the name, and the transfer completes once the request is approved or the waiting period passes.',
			'Under the ICANN Transfer Policy, the current registrar has up to five days to respond, and it may email the registrant to confirm or reject the move. Approving that email promptly can shorten the wait.',
			array( 'h3' => 'Domain transfer requirements' ),
			array(
				'The name must be more than 60 days old and must not have been transferred in the last 60 days, under ICANN rules.',
